# Expense Tracker Frontend Documentation

## Project Title

Expense Tracker Frontend Application

---

# 1. Introduction

The Expense Tracker Frontend Application is a web-based user interface 
developed using Python and Streamlit. It allows users to manage daily expenses 
efficiently by interacting with backend REST APIs.

The application provides the following functionalities:

* Add new expenses
* View all expenses
* Update existing expenses
* Delete expenses
* View expense summary by category

The frontend communicates with the backend server using HTTP requests.

---

# 2. Technologies Used

| Technology | Purpose                |
| ---------- | ---------------------- |
| Python     | Programming Language   |
| Streamlit  | Frontend Web Framework |
| Requests   | API Communication      |
| Pandas     | Data Handling & Tables |

---

# 3. Project Structure

```plaintext
frontend/
│
├── app.py
├── requirements.txt
└── .streamlit/
    └── secrets.toml
```

---

# 4. Requirements

Install all required libraries using:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

# 5. Required Libraries

The following libraries are used:

```python
streamlit
requests
pandas
```

---

# 6. Backend Configuration

The backend server URL is stored securely using Streamlit secrets.

Example:

```toml
be_server_url = "https://your-backend-url.com"
```

Accessed in code using:

```python
server = st.secrets["be_server_url"]
```

---

# 7. Application Features

## 7.1 Add Expense

This module allows users to add new expenses.

### Input Fields

* Title
* Amount
* Category
* Payment Method
* Expense Date
* Description

### API Used

```http
POST /add_expense
```

### Payload Example

```json
{
  "title": "Lunch",
  "amount": 250,
  "category": "Food",
  "payment_method": "UPI",
  "expense_date": "2026-05-28",
  "description": "Lunch with friends"
}
```

### Functionality

* Collects user input
* Sends POST request to backend
* Displays success or error message

---

## 7.2 View Expenses

Displays all saved expenses in table format.

### API Used

```http
GET /get_expenses
```

### Features

* Shows all expense records
* Displays total expense amount
* Uses Pandas DataFrame for tabular display

### Output Example

| ID | Title | Amount | Category |
| -- | ----- | ------ | -------- |
| 1  | Lunch | 250    | Food     |

---

## 7.3 Update Expense

Allows updating an existing expense.

### Process

1. Enter Expense ID
2. Fetch existing data
3. Edit fields
4. Submit updated information

### APIs Used

```http
GET /get_single_expense/{id}
PUT /update_expense/{id}
```

### Features

* Pre-fills existing expense data
* Updates selected expense
* Uses session state for temporary storage

---

## 7.4 Delete Expense

Deletes an expense using Expense ID.

### API Used

```http
DELETE /delete_expense/{id}
```

### Features

* Removes expense permanently
* Displays confirmation message

---

## 7.5 Expense Summary

Displays category-wise expense summary.

### API Used

```http
GET /expense_summary
```

### Features

* Shows category-wise totals
* Displays bar chart visualization
* Uses Streamlit charts

---

# 8. Streamlit Components Used

| Component              | Purpose            |
| ---------------------- | ------------------ |
| st.title()             | Page Title         |
| st.header()            | Section Headers    |
| st.sidebar.selectbox() | Navigation Menu    |
| st.text_input()        | User Input         |
| st.number_input()      | Numeric Input      |
| st.selectbox()         | Dropdown Selection |
| st.date_input()        | Date Selection     |
| st.text_area()         | Multi-line Text    |
| st.button()            | Trigger Actions    |
| st.dataframe()         | Display Tables     |
| st.bar_chart()         | Display Charts     |
| st.success()           | Success Messages   |
| st.error()             | Error Messages     |
| st.warning()           | Warning Messages   |

---

# 9. Error Handling

The application uses:

```python
try:
    ...
except Exception as e:
    st.error(str(e))
```

This ensures:

* Proper exception handling
* Better user experience
* API error visibility

---

# 10. Session State Usage

The application uses Streamlit Session State for storing fetched expense data temporarily.

Example:

```python
st.session_state["expense_data"] = data
```

Purpose:

* Maintains data during reruns
* Helps in updating expense forms

---

# Updated Deployment Section — Streamlit Cloud

# 11. Deployment Using Streamlit Cloud

The Expense Tracker Frontend Application is deployed using Streamlit Cloud, 
which allows easy hosting and sharing of Streamlit applications online.

---

## 11.1 Prerequisites

Before deployment, ensure the following:

* GitHub repository contains frontend files
* `app.py` is present
* `requirements.txt` contains all required libraries
* Backend API is already deployed and accessible
* Streamlit Cloud account is available

---

## 11.2 Required Files

Project structure:

```plaintext id="c9o9b9"
frontend/
│
├── app.py
├── requirements.txt
└── .streamlit/
    └── secrets.toml
```

---

## 11.3 requirements.txt

Example:

```txt id="y8n5jk"
streamlit
requests
pandas
```

---

## 11.4 Backend URL Configuration

Sensitive information such as backend URL is stored securely using Streamlit Secrets.

Example:

```toml id="e7h8vs"
be_server_url = "https://your-backend-api-url.com"
```

Accessed in application:

```python id="a6z2kl"
server = st.secrets["be_server_url"]
```

---

## 11.5 Deployment Steps

### Step 1: Push Code to GitHub

Upload all frontend project files to a GitHub repository.

---

### Step 2: Open Streamlit Cloud

Visit:

[https://share.streamlit.io/](https://share.streamlit.io/)

Login using GitHub account.

---

### Step 3: Create New App

Click:

```plaintext id="u2h9yo"
New App
```

---

### Step 4: Select Repository

Choose:

* GitHub Repository
* Branch
* `app.py` file

---

### Step 5: Add Secrets

In Streamlit Cloud:

```plaintext id="m8q7xa"
Settings → Secrets
```

Add:

```toml id="u1j4pi"
be_server_url = "https://your-backend-api-url.com"
```

---

### Step 6: Deploy Application

Click:

```plaintext id="t4s8md"
Deploy
```

Streamlit Cloud automatically installs dependencies and hosts the application.

---

## 11.6 Deployment Features

Benefits of using Streamlit Cloud:

* Free hosting
* Easy deployment
* Automatic GitHub integration
* Fast updates after GitHub push
* Secure secrets management
* Public shareable URL

---

## 11.7 Updating the Application

To update the deployed app:

1. Modify code locally
2. Push changes to GitHub
3. Streamlit Cloud automatically redeploys the application

---

## 11.8 Common Deployment Errors

| Error                 | Reason               | Solution                             |
| --------------------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| ModuleNotFoundError   | Missing package      | Add package to requirements.txt      |
| Secrets Error         | Missing secrets      | Configure secrets in Streamlit Cloud |
| API Connection Failed | Backend not running  | Verify backend deployment            |
| App Crash             | Syntax/runtime error | Check deployment logs                |

---

## 11.9 Deployment URL

After successful deployment, Streamlit Cloud generates a public URL such as:

```plaintext id="o58x6f"
https://your-app-name.streamlit.app
```

Users can access the Expense Tracker application through this URL.


---

# 12. How to Run the Application Locally

## Step 1: Clone Repository

```bash
git clone <repository-url>
```

## Step 2: Navigate to Project Folder

```bash
cd frontend
```

## Step 3: Install Requirements

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Step 4: Run Application

```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

